Why Work at Mercer Advisors?

For more than 40 years, Mercer Advisors has been helping families amplify and simplify their financial lives by integrating financial planning, investment management, business management, tax, estate, insurance, and more, all managed by a single team. We deliver the kind of comprehensive care once reserved for only the wealthiest households.

Today, we serve over 42,800+ families across 110+ cities across the U.S. Ranked the #1 RIA Firm in the nation by Barron’s for two consecutive years, Mercer Advisors is an independent fiduciary legally bound to act in our clients’ best interests - always.*

Mercer Advisors offers a workplace that stands apart in the financial industry. More than half of our employees and client-facing professionals are women, reflecting the clients we serve. With a flexible, national footprint, we build our teams around exceptional talent - wherever they are.

Join us and help families amplify and simplify their financial lives with confidence.

* Mercer Advisors was ranked #1 for RIA firms with up to $70 billion in assets. The Barron’s top RIA ranking is based on a combination of metrics - including size, growth, service quality, technology, succession planning and others. No fee was paid for participation in the ranking, however, Mercer Advisors has paid a fee to Barron’s to use the ranking in marketing. Please see important information about the ranking criteria methodology&nbsp; here .

Job Summary:

The Product Support Specialist serves as a critical member of the Product Support team, providing exceptional technical and client support across Mercer Advisors’ technology ecosystem. This role acts as a primary point of contact for advisors, employees, and clients, delivering timely resolution of system issues, managing Client Portal support requests, and ensuring a high-quality user experience across multiple platforms.&nbsp;

The Product Support Specialist combines technical troubleshooting expertise with a concierge-level service approach to support business operations and client engagement. Responsibilities include managing support requests through ticketing systems, maintaining user access, partnering with third-party vendors, documenting solutions and processes, and collaborating with Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to identify opportunities for system enhancements and process improvements.&nbsp;

Success in this role requires strong analytical skills, exceptional communication, a client-centric mindset, and the ability to effectively prioritize work in a fast-paced environment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

While this role is remote, we have a strong preference for candidates in the Pacific or Mountain Time Zones given the team's current needs.

&nbsp;

Essential Job Functions for this role include:

Client Support &amp; Service Excellence&nbsp;

• Serve as the primary point of contact for Client Portal and technology-related inquiries received through phone, email, and ticketing channels.&nbsp;

• Deliver a concierge-level support experience by providing prompt, professional, and proactive&nbsp;assistance&nbsp;to advisors, employees, and clients.&nbsp;

• Guide users through system functionality, troubleshoot issues, and ensure&nbsp;timely&nbsp;resolution of requests&nbsp;in accordance with&nbsp;established service level agreements (SLAs).&nbsp;

• Educate users on platform capabilities, best practices, and available self-service resources.&nbsp;

• Maintain&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;records of client interactions, issue resolutions, and support activities.&nbsp;

• Take ownership of support cases from&nbsp;initial&nbsp;intake through final resolution, ensuring consistent communication and follow-through throughout the process.&nbsp;

Technical Support &amp; Platform Administration&nbsp;

• Provide day-to-day support for various business technology platforms and applications.&nbsp;

• Configure and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;user accounts, permissions, and system access requests.

